Lower the minimum xHE-AAC bit rate of the open-source fdk-xhe-aac (for Dream's DRM use)

The open-source encoder only has the "DASH" configuration table, which starts at
12 kbit/s mono and 16 kbit/s stereo (rates in 2 kbit/s steps). The same tools work lower:
mono 4, 6, 8 and 10 kbit/s and stereo 12 kbit/s were encoded and decoded back with
Dream's xHE-AAC receive path (tone test; speech/music quality at the low rates has
not been assessed). Stereo 8 and 10 kbit/s are not possible (encoder open fails).

Apply in the root of the fdk-aac tree: git apply <this file>   (the lines above the diff are ignored)
Mono 4 kbit/s also needs the first row of the quad rate SBR tuning table (sbr_main.c) opened: it started at
6 kbit/s and made Open fail with an internal SBR error.

